"description" = "Horula is a clock that plans across time zones. Slide one control and every city you follow moves with it, so finding an hour that works in Vancouver, London and Tokyo takes a second.\n\nWORLD CLOCK\n- See whether the sun is up in each city, worked out from its real sunrise and sunset.\n- Slide the planner in 15 minute steps to line up a meeting across cities.\n- Tap a city for its sunrise, sunset and hours of daylight.\n- An analog face whose second hand sweeps instead of ticks.\n- On the Mac, a world map shows where it is day and where it is night.\n\nALARMS\n- Alarms ring with the app closed, the phone locked or on silent.\n- Skip just the next ring of a repeating alarm when you sleep in.\n- Pick a snooze length from 1 to 15 minutes.\n- A bedtime and wake up schedule that counts your hours of sleep.\n\nSTOPWATCH AND TIMERS\n- A stopwatch with laps, best and worst marked. Tap the time for an analog dial with a lap hand.\n- Copy your laps as a table.\n- Run several timers at once; each shows on the Lock Screen and rings when it ends.\n- Pin the timers you use as presets. Recent timers restart with one tap.\n- Interval timers count work and rest rounds for you.\n\nEVERYWHERE YOU LOOK\n- Apple Watch: your cities, the stopwatch and your timers on your wrist.\n- Widgets for the Home Screen, Lock Screen and StandBy: your cities and your next alarm.\n- A nightstand mode with big digits that dim at night and keep the screen awake.\n- On the Mac too, with Command 1 to 4 for tabs.\n- In twelve languages.\n\nYOURS\n- No account, no ads, no tracking. Everything stays on your device.\n- Export a backup and import it on another device, or in Horula on the web at horula.jaybulb.com.";
"keywords" = "alarm,timer,stopwatch,world clock,time zone,sunrise,sunset,nightstand,meeting,interval,widget";
"promotionalText" = "Plan a meeting across time zones with one slider. Alarms that ring with the app closed, interval timers, Apple Watch and a nightstand mode.";
